    "title": "pandas.Series.to_frame — pandas 2.2.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Series.to_frame#\n\n- \nSeries.to_frame(*name=<no_default>* )[source]#\n- Convert Series to DataFrame. \n  - Parameters:\n    - **name** object, optional\n    - The passed name should substitute for the series name (if it has one).\n  - Returns:\n    - DataFrame\n    - DataFrame representation of Series.\n Examples >>> s = pd.Series([\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"], ... name=\"vals\") >>> s.to_frame() vals 0 a 1 b 2 c",
    "markdown_length": 400,
